  "tagline": "Header-only C++ HNSW library with Python bindings, from the authors of the HNSW algorithm.",
  "description": "hnswlib is the reference implementation of Hierarchical Navigable Small World graphs, maintained under the nmslib organisation with contributions from HNSW co-author Yury Malkov. It is a small header-only C++ library with Python bindings that supports incremental inserts, deletions via marking, filtering callbacks and saving/loading indexes, using L2, inner product or cosine distance. Many early vector databases and RAG tools embedded it directly, and it remains a common baseline. It is a library with no metadata store or server, and releases are infrequent (0.9.0 in March 2026, 0.10 in release candidates).",
